{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788975783,"nonce":"RwdcexPB5Bl6tUb+13gYThOmt14=","title":"Interpreter treats OEndTrap's operand as a register and clears r0/r1","message":"HL's `OEndTrap` operand is a bool flag (`OEndTrap of bool`), not a register --\nhashlink's jit.c never reads it and just pops `trap_current`. `ash_interp`'s\n`Opcode::EndTrap` arm does `registers.set(exc.0, null)`, so it nulls r1 (or r0\nwhen the flag is 0) after every `try` block.\n\nLatent: no test program keeps anything live in r0/r1 across an `EndTrap`. It is\na miscompile waiting for one that does. The AIR serializer already preserves the\nflag verbatim rather than inventing a register, and the JIT correctly ignores it.","files":null}]}